      "raw_text": "To find the total amount of tea at the beginning of the party, we need to calculate the total amount consumed by the students and add it to the amount remaining.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the amount of tea consumed by the first group of students.**\nThere are 4 students who each drank 1.5 quarts.\n$$4 \\text{ students} \\times 1.5 \\text{ quarts/student} = 6 \\text{ quarts}$$\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the amount of tea consumed by the second group of students.**\nThere are 16 students who each drank 2 quarts.\n$$16 \\text{ students} \\times 2 \\text{ quarts/student} = 32 \\text{ quarts}$$\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the total amount of tea consumed.**\nAdd the consumption from both groups together.\n$$6 \\text{ quarts} + 32 \\text{ quarts} = 38 \\text{ quarts}$$\n\n**Step 4: Calculate the total amount of tea at the beginning.**\nAdd the remaining tea to the total consumed.\n$$\\text{Remaining tea} = 10 \\text{ quarts}$$\n$$\\text{Total tea} = \\text{Consumed tea} + \\text{Remaining tea}$$\n$$\\text{Total tea} = 38 \\text{ quarts} + 10 \\text{ quarts} = 48 \\text{ quarts}$$\n\n**Step 5: Convert the total amount from quarts to gallons.**\nWe know that 1 gallon is equal to 4 quarts. To convert quarts to gallons, divide by 4.\n$$48 \\text{ quarts} \\div 4 \\text{ quarts/gallon} = 12 \\text{ gallons}$$\n\n#### 12<|im_end|>",
      "answer_text": "To find the total amount of tea at the beginning of the party, we need to calculate the total amount consumed by the students and add it to the amount remaining.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the amount of tea consumed by the first group of students.**\nThere are 4 students who each drank 1.5 quarts.\n$$4 \\text{ students} \\times 1.5 \\text{ quarts/student} = 6 \\text{ quarts}$$\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the amount of tea consumed by the second group of students.**\nThere are 16 students who each drank 2 quarts.\n$$16 \\text{ students} \\times 2 \\text{ quarts/student} = 32 \\text{ quarts}$$\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the total amount of tea consumed.**\nAdd the consumption from both groups together.\n$$6 \\text{ quarts} + 32 \\text{ quarts} = 38 \\text{ quarts}$$\n\n**Step 4: Calculate the total amount of tea at the beginning.**\nAdd the remaining tea to the total consumed.\n$$\\text{Remaining tea} = 10 \\text{ quarts}$$\n$$\\text{Total tea} = \\text{Consumed tea} + \\text{Remaining tea}$$\n$$\\text{Total tea} = 38 \\text{ quarts} + 10 \\text{ quarts} = 48 \\text{ quarts}$$\n\n**Step 5: Convert the total amount from quarts to gallons.**\nWe know that 1 gallon is equal to 4 quarts. To convert quarts to gallons, divide by 4.\n$$48 \\text{ quarts} \\div 4 \\text{ quarts/gallon} = 12 \\text{ gallons}$$\n\n#### 12",
